%% Atomic Commits payment flows - architecture target and current dev snapshot.
%% Snapshot: 23 October 2026. Production-target sections describe planned behavior.
%% The CURRENT DEV section is the delivered implementation, not a settled payment flow.
%% JWT migration: issue #4. Separate migration/runtime DB configuration: issue #3.
%% Implemented SDK wrapper: backend/src/services/open-payments.ts.
%% Implemented manual command: backend/src/commands/wallet-lookup.ts.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CLI as Temporary dev CLI
    actor User as Customer
    participant Phone as Customer Flutter app
    participant Merchant as Merchant Flutter app
    participant API as Atomic Commits API
    participant SDK as Backend Open Payments SDK
    participant DB as Supabase / protected storage
    participant Provider as Payment account provider

    Note over User,Provider: PRODUCTION TARGET - planned architecture, not current functionality.<br/>The CURRENT DEV section below identifies what is implemented today.
    Note over API,SDK: Target: reuse a server-side SDK client for the integration.<br/>Its developer signing key identifies Atomic Commits.<br/>Payer wallets and approved provider grant tokens are selected per operation.
    Note over Phone,Provider: Separate credentials: app login credential, backend developer key,<br/>provider spending grant, and the phone's future offline-signing key.

    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
        Note over User,Provider: PRODUCTION TARGET - app signup and wallet linking
        User->>Phone: Sign up or log in to Atomic Commits
        Phone->>API: App authentication over HTTPS
        API->>DB: Save or verify BCrypt password hash and app user
        API-->>Phone: App login credential - JWT migration is planned in issue #4
        Note over Phone: Native app login credentials use platform-protected storage.

        alt Customer already has a provider wallet
            User->>Phone: Enter wallet address or payment pointer
        else Customer needs a provider account or wallet
            Phone-->>User: Open provider-hosted account onboarding
            User->>Provider: Complete provider signup, wallet creation and funding
            User->>Phone: Return with the provider wallet address
            Note over Phone,Provider: Account opening needs provider support or an external provider flow.<br/>A public API for automatic consumer account creation has not been established here.
        end

        Phone->>API: Begin linking a wallet for the authenticated app user
        API->>API: Validate the wallet URL and block internal/private-network fetches
        API->>SDK: Get public wallet metadata
        SDK->>Provider: GET wallet address
        Provider-->>SDK: Wallet ID, asset, scale, auth server and resource server
        SDK-->>API: Validated public metadata
        API->>DB: Save short-lived, one-use wallet-link interaction state
        API->>SDK: Start an interactive subject-verification grant
        SDK->>Provider: Signed ownership-verification request
        Provider-->>SDK: Provider interaction URL and continuation details
        SDK-->>API: Provider interaction and continuation details
        API-->>Phone: Open the provider interaction in a browser
        User->>Provider: Authenticate and approve wallet verification
        Provider-->>API: Browser redirect callback
        API->>API: Verify correlation, interaction hash, expiry and one-use state
        API->>SDK: Continue the grant
        SDK->>Provider: Signed continuation request
        Provider-->>SDK: Verified subject
        SDK-->>API: Verified subject result
        API->>API: Require the verified subject to match the claimed wallet
        API->>DB: Save VERIFIED wallet link under this app user
        API-->>Phone: Show connected wallet and its asset
        Note over Phone,DB: Repeat linking for additional wallets and choose sending/receiving defaults.<br/>Wallet links belong to users, not global sender/receiver environment variables.
        Note over API,Provider: Public metadata is discovery. Ownership verification establishes the link.<br/>Permission to spend is a separate provider-approved grant.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 250, 235)
        Note over User,Provider: PRODUCTION TARGET - online provider payment
        Phone->>API: Authenticated payment request with amount, merchant ID and idempotency key
        API->>DB: Resolve verified payer and merchant wallet links
        API->>API: Enforce user ownership, recipient authorization and amount/asset rules
        API->>DB: Atomically reserve the payment attempt, then commit
        Note over API,DB: Do not hold a database transaction open during external provider calls.

        API->>SDK: Obtain incoming-payment grant and create recipient incoming payment
        SDK->>Provider: Signed incoming-payment grant and resource requests
        Provider-->>SDK: Incoming payment ID
        SDK-->>API: Incoming payment reference
        API->>SDK: Obtain quote grant and create a fresh quote from the payer
        SDK->>Provider: Quote the incoming payment
        Provider-->>SDK: Quote ID, debit amount, receive amount and assets/scales
        SDK-->>API: Provider quote including conversion and fees
        Note over API,Provider: Amounts use integer minor-unit strings with explicit asset/scale.<br/>Check debit limits against the quoted debit amount, including fees and FX.

        alt A suitable prior outgoing-payment grant is valid and within budget
            API->>DB: Load and decrypt the grant bound to this payer and wallet
        else Fresh payer consent is required
            API->>SDK: Request a bounded outgoing-payment grant
            SDK->>Provider: Signed grant request for the intended payer wallet
            Provider-->>SDK: Provider consent URL and continuation details
            SDK-->>API: Provider consent and continuation details
            API-->>Phone: Redirect the payer to the provider
            User->>Provider: Approve the displayed spending limits
            Provider-->>API: Browser redirect callback
            API->>API: Verify callback correlation, interaction hash and one-use state
            API->>SDK: Continue the approved grant
            SDK->>Provider: Signed continuation request
            Provider-->>SDK: Finalized provider grant and access token
            SDK-->>API: Grant token, scope and limits
            API->>DB: Encrypt any persisted token and save payer-bound grant metadata
        end

        API->>API: Recheck quote, grant scope, expiry and remaining debit budget
        API->>SDK: Create outgoing payment with payer wallet, fresh quote and payer grant token
        SDK->>Provider: Signed outgoing-payment request
        Provider-->>SDK: Provider payment ID and current state
        SDK-->>API: Provider resource references
        API->>DB: Save real resource IDs and PROCESSING state
        API->>SDK: Retrieve and reconcile authoritative payment outcome
        SDK->>Provider: Read payment resources by their provider IDs
        Provider-->>SDK: Current authoritative outcome
        SDK-->>API: Provider outcome

        alt Provider confirms successful completion
            API->>DB: Save SUCCEEDED and actual payment amounts
            API-->>Phone: Confirmed payment
            API-->>Merchant: Confirmed receipt
        else Provider confirms failure
            API->>DB: Save FAILED with a safe failure reason
            API-->>Phone: Payment failed
            API-->>Merchant: Payment failed
        else Pending, timeout or ambiguous result
            API->>DB: Preserve the attempt claim and save PROCESSING or UNKNOWN
            API-->>Phone: Pending / reconciling
            API-->>Merchant: Pending / reconciling
            Note over API,Provider: Reconcile the existing attempt before any new debit.<br/>API acceptance or a local database row is not provider-confirmed settlement.
        end
        Note over DB,Provider: The account provider holds and moves funds.<br/>Supabase stores app records and provider references, not an invented funds ledger.
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 220)
        Note over User,Provider: CONDITIONAL PRODUCTION TARGET - payer offline, merchant online<br/>Enable only after proving provider support for reusable, budget-limited grants.<br/>Required proof: two fresh payments using one approved grant without a second consent prompt.
        Note over Phone,Provider: Initial wallet linking, device enrollment and provider spending consent happen online.<br/>A device signature is separate from the backend developer key and provider permission.
        Phone->>Phone: Generate a per-device Ed25519 key pair and securely retain the private key
        Phone->>API: Authenticated enrollment of the public key and device ID
        API->>DB: Save public verification key, owner and revocation state
        Note over API,DB: A usable prior payer-approved grant must already be available.<br/>Token expiry, revocation and aggregate provider spending limits remain authoritative.

        User->>Phone: Confirm a spending ceiling and Quick or Errand lifetime
        Phone->>Phone: Sign a versioned instruction with fresh nonce, payer/device, asset,<br/>ceiling, issued-at, expiry, mode and optional merchant restriction
        Note over Phone: Quick: at most 30 seconds.<br/>Errand: user-selected duration, at most 25 minutes.<br/>The private signing key stays on the device.
        Phone-->>Merchant: Present the signed QR or a printed QR while the payer is offline
        Merchant->>API: Authenticated merchant submits the QR, actual charge and recipient identity
        API->>DB: Resolve the enrolled public key and verified merchant wallet
        API->>API: Verify signature, device status, mode/lifetime, clock bounds,<br/>asset/amount constraints and merchant restriction
        API->>DB: Atomically claim the unique device/nonce and payment attempt, then commit

        alt Prior provider grant is usable for this payer and new payment
            API->>SDK: Create fresh incoming payment and quote, enforce quoted debit ceilings,<br/>then execute with the payer's existing approved grant
            SDK->>Provider: Signed provider requests within the remaining grant budget
            Provider-->>SDK: Payment resource references and outcome
            SDK-->>API: Provider results
            Note over API,Provider: Use the same confirmation and reconciliation path as the online flow.<br/>Exactly one successful redemption consumes the whole credential.<br/>Only the actual permitted charge is paid, not automatically the whole ceiling.
            API-->>Merchant: Confirmed, failed or pending according to provider outcome
        else Provider requires renewed payer interaction or usable permission is absent
            API-->>Merchant: Payer must reconnect and authorize before settlement
        end
        Note over Phone,Provider: A QR does not reserve funds or guarantee sufficient balance.<br/>If both devices are offline, any queued action is pending only.<br/>If reusable grants are unsupported, keep the online payment flow as the MVP fallback.
    end

    rect rgb(255, 235, 235)
        Note over CLI,Provider: CURRENT DEV - implemented SDK bootstrap and public wallet lookup only
        CLI->>CLI: Read one/two command arguments or temporary SENDING/RECEIVING environment values
        CLI->>SDK: lookupWalletAddresses - normalize pointers and create a public client
        SDK->>Provider: Public wallet-address GET requests with SDK response validation
        Provider-->>SDK: Public wallet metadata
        SDK-->>CLI: Wallet IDs, assets/scales and provider server URLs
        CLI->>CLI: Print mode = temporary-integration-lookup and metadata

        Note over API,SDK: createOpenPaymentsClient is a factory that returns a new signing-capable client.<br/>It loads CLIENT_WALLET_ADDRESS_URL, KEY_ID and PRIVATE_KEY_PATH.<br/>The current public lookup command does not use the signing key.
        Note over CLI,SDK: DEV identity: a demo payer Test Wallet supplies the integration identity/key.<br/>Local .env and PEM files are plaintext and excluded from Git.<br/>Production developer keys belong in backend secret storage, not Flutter.
        Note over API,DB: CURRENT: BCrypt passwords, PostgreSQL cookie sessions and verified DB TLS.<br/>JWT migration is tracked in issue #4. DB connection split is deferred in issue #3.
        Note over Phone,DB: NOT IMPLEMENTED: Flutter signup/wallet linking and its server URL/SSRF controls,<br/>verified user wallet records, provider grant persistence/encryption,<br/>payment execution/reconciliation, phone key enrollment and signed offline redemption.
        Note over CLI,Provider: Current provider: Interledger Test Wallet with simulated funds and manual funding.<br/>Wallet metadata, matching registered developer keys and SDK initialization are verified.<br/>The single-transfer proof and reusable-grant proof are still pending.
    end
